      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks, that's a good start. I'm worried it might sound a little bit too generic or \"templatey\" though. Could you try making it sound a bit more personal and warm? Like, acknowledge that we really enjoyed the conversation and that it was a tough call, without losing that professional edge? Maybe add a line about how we'll keep his resume on file for future openings that might be a better match for his specific background.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here's a revised draft that aims to add a bit more warmth and personality to the email:\n\nDear Marcus,\n\nI wanted to personally reach out to you regarding the Senior Developer position at our Austin office. I'm sure you're aware that we had a tough decision to make, but I wanted to take a moment to express my gratitude for the time you took to speak with us. Your passion for software development and your impressive technical skills truly shone through during our conversation, and we were all impressed by your energy and enthusiasm.\n\nAfter careful consideration, we've decided to move forward with another candidate whose experience aligns more closely with our specific cloud architecture needs. Please know that this decision was not made lightly, and we were genuinely impressed by your qualifications and potential. However, we have to prioritize the needs of our organization, and this candidate's experience is a better fit for our team at this time.\n\nI want to assure you that we were thoroughly charmed by your conversation, and we're so sorry that we couldn't make it work out. You reminded us of the importance of collaboration and creative problem-solving, and we appreciate the time you took to share your insights with us. We're confident that you'll find a great fit elsewhere, and we",
